    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/compliance-security-administrator-i-ii-iii-or-senior-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Compliance & Security Administrator I, II, III, or Senior",
      "description": "Compliance & Security Administrator I, II, III, or Senior - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Compliance & Security Administrator I, II, III, or Senior 511247 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 493000 - Research Compliance and Security Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: This position serves as a member of a team of professionals responsible for ensuring that Mississippi State University maintains compliance with federal regulations related to research compliance, research security, and export control. This position provides administrative oversight and operational support across a broad range of compliance and security areas, including human and animal research protections, biosafety, financial conflicts of interest, controlled substances, responsible conduct of research, and export control programs. The position supports university-wide programs and works collaboratively with compliance leadership, including the Research Compliance Officer, Facility Security Officer, and Export Control Officer, to ensure institutional compliance and risk mitigation. Rankings and qualifications within levels (I, II, III, Senior) are based on education and experience. Salary Grade :  14 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Research Compliance Functions • Implement and support policies and procedures related to IRB, IACUC, IBC, RCR, FCOI, and controlled substances. • Review compliance applications, facilitate revisions, and coordinate submission materials for committee review. • Notify investigators of committee decisions and request additional information as needed. • Assist with agenda preparation, meeting coordination, and documentation of compliance committee meetings. • Support accreditation programs (e.g., AAHRPP, AAALAC) and maintain required documentation. • Conduct or support post-approval monitoring and quality assurance activities. • Recommend improvements to policies, procedures, and standard operating processes. • Provide guidance to researchers by interpreting applicable federal regulations and agency requirements. Research Security & Export Control Functions • Track export control training, monitor expirations, and notify personnel of renewal requirements. • Process and document Technology Control Plan (TCP) requirements, including personnel access approvals. • Maintain records for export-controlled projects and associated compliance documentation. • Monitor personnel changes (e.g., termination reports) impacting export-controlled access. • Verify compliance requirements such as citizenship status, visa eligibility, and training completion. • Coordinate TCP execution and documentation processes. • Assist with export-controlled financial monitoring and validation of personnel charges to projects. • Support review and coordination of security-related applications (e.g., Official Visitor Application processes). General Responsibilities • Maintain accurate and complete compliance and security records. • Educate faculty, staff, and students to promote a culture of compliance and research security. • Interact professionally with internal stakeholders and external regulatory bodies. • Perform other duties aligned with the mission of the Office of Research Compliance & Security. Minimum Qualifications: Compliance and Security Administrator I: Bachelor’s Degree in a related field. One year of relevant experience. Compliance and Security Administrator II: Bachelor’s Degree in a related field. Three years of relevant experience. Experience must include at least 2 years at the preceding level. Compliance and Security Administrator III: Bachelor’s Degree in a related field. Five years of relevant experience. Experience must include at least 2 years at the preceding level. Senior Compliance and Security Administrator: Master’s Degree, Ph.D., or Juris Doctor and a Professional Certification related to Research Compliance or Research Security (e.g., CIP, CPIA, CRA, ECoP, ISP) Seven years of relevant experience. Experience must include at least 2 years at the preceding level. Substitution Allowed: Bachelor’s degree is required; no substitutions allowed. When a candidate has the required education but lacks the required experience, they may apply additional relevant education toward the experience requirement at a rate of one (1) year education per year of required experience. When a candidate lacks an advanced degree, two years of additional experience may be substituted for a master’s degree for the position of Senior Compliance and Security Administrator. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Knowledge of research compliance frameworks and research security requirements. • Familiarity with applicable research compliance regulations (OHRP, FDA, OLAW, USDA, FDA, etc.) and export control regulations (EAR, ITAR, OFAC). • Strong analytical, organizational, and problem-solving skills. • Ability to interpret regulatory requirements and apply them operationally. • Strong written and verbal communication skills. • Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines in a dynamic environment. • Experience with data management and enterprise systems. • High level of integrity, confidentiality, and professionalism. Working Conditions and Physical Effort 1. No unusual physical requirements. 2. Requires no heavy lifting, and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. 3. Frequent - Externally imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; irregular hours may be anticipated; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position. 4. Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. 5. Job requires standing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting up to 10 pounds. 6. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. 7. Hearing requirements: Heavy telephone contact requires ability to hear and respond to telephone conversations. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Recommended Jobs Business Manager I, II, or III Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Manages and coordinates the business operations of a department/unit.  Performs duties required to maintain and administer departmental budgets; administers staff policies and/or procedures; compiles reports; performs administrative procedures. Research Associate I (L,P,S) Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Gout lab (https://sites.google.com/view/goutlab/home) is hiring a Research Associate in\ncomputational biology to work on two NIH-funded projects in collaboration with the Vermulst lab at University of Southern California (USC). The first project (1R01AG083065) is focused on the potential role of transcription errors on the formation of amyloid and prion-like proteins. The second project is about temporal control of mitochondrial mutagenesis (1R01AG075130-\n01). The candidate will be based in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University, in Starkville, MS (USA) and will collaborate extensively with the Vermulst lab at USC. Postdoctoral Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi An NSF-funded postdoc position is available in the lab of Megan Smith in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University. The project aims to develop robust, user-friendly machine learning tools for population genetic inference and to apply these tools to uncover the drivers of diversification in several empirical systems. The lab has developed a Python package for demographic inference using machine learning, and the successful candidate will extend these methods along several axes.\n\nIn addition to the current project, the lab is pursuing a wide range of empirical and computational research in phylogenetics and population genetics. To learn more about our work visit https://www.meganlsmith.org Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance , 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762 Copyright © 2026 Mississippi State University. All Rights Reserved. Technical problems, contact the Service Desk . Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/research-associate-i-miami-fl-florida-united-states": {
      "title": "Research Associate I",
      "description": "Research Associate I - Miami, FL, Florida, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Research Associate I 511221 Miami, FL Florida 191001 - Northern Gulf Institute Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The primary function of this position will be supporting software development and data analysis within the NOAA ARGO program. This includes supporting the end-to-end lifecycle of NOAA Argo data, from real-time ingestion to the dissemination of research-quality products. Specifically, the selected candidate will develop and maintain high-performance software across multi-language environments to ensure 24/7 operational reliability; implement rigorous documentation standards to ensure system continuity and technical transparency; accelerate the transition of experimental scripts into hardened operational workflows; and uphold international FAIR (Findable, Accessible, Interoperable, Reusable) data principles, ensuring all software development meets modern global standards for data integrity and accessibility. Salary Grade :  13 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Northern Gulf Institute (NGI) is a National Oceanic and Atmospheric Administration (NOAA) Cooperative Institute comprised of six academic institutions that are geographically distributed across the U.S. Gulf Coast states. The six NGI member institutions are Mississippi State University (lead), the University of Southern Mississippi, Florida State University, Louisiana State University, the University of Alabama in Huntsville, and the Dauphin Island Sea Laboratory. Together with NOAA and in support of their strategic plan, NGI conducts research on interconnections among Gulf of Mexico environments, habitats, resources, and people and engages in outreach to help others learn about and make decisions based on these interconnections. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Delivering high-reliability software suites and production-grade applications supported by rigorous, FAIR-compliant documentation and maintenance schedules for the ARGO program • Transitioning experimental scripts into stable, transparent operational workflows that ensure global data integrity and accessibility. Minimum Qualifications: Grade and salary will be commensurate with individual’s background, education and experience. Beginning with a bachelor’s degree: A professional employee with a bachelor’s degree in Engineering or related field and demonstrated competence can begin work at the Research/Extension Associate I level. To begin at the Research/Extension Associate II level, one must have a bachelor’s degree in the required discipline and a minimum of three years relevant experience and the equivalent of a master’s degree. To begin at the Research/Extension Associate III level, one must have a bachelor’s degree in the required discipline and a minimum of six years relevant experience and the equivalent of the master’s degree. Beginning with a master’s degree: A professional employee with a master’s degree in Engineering or related field, one year of relevant experience and demonstrated competence can begin work at the Research/Extension Associate II level. To begin at the Research/Extension Associate III level, one must have a master’s degree in the required discipline and a minimum of three years relevant experience and the equivalent of a master’s degree. To begin at the Senior Research/Extension Associate level, one must have a master’s degree in the required discipline and a minimum of six years relevant experience. Beginning with a doctoral degree: A professional employee with a doctoral degree in Engineering or related field with two years of relevant experience and demonstrated competence can begin work at the Research/Extension Associate III level. To begin at the Senior Research/Extension Associate level, one must have a doctoral degree in the required discipline and a minimum of three years relevant experience. Preferred Qualifications: • Experience in Data Analysis • Experience in Software Development • Basic Knowledge in Oceanography Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Familiarity with Linux and Phyton • Work well in a collaborative team environment or individually • Be willing to work in a range of environmental conditions • Desire to work with a range of datasets and applications • Strong interpersonal, communication skills and the ability to work effectively with a wide range of constituencies • Ability to coordinate multiple projects simultaneously • Strong attention to detail Working Conditions and Physical Effort Occasional and/or light lifting required. Limited exposure to elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc., but none to the point of being disagreeable. May involve minor safety hazards where likely result would be cuts, bruises, etc. Routine deadlines, usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressure from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires standing, walking, climbing or balancing, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling and lifting up to 50 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically, ability to distinguish colors. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Apply online by submitting a cover letter, resume, and a copy of your transcript(s). Any social security numbers included on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 2d1789bd Last Name (required) c533e953 Email (required) 3a6c4ed4 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Business Manager I, II, or III Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Manages and coordinates the business operations of a department/unit.  Performs duties required to maintain and administer departmental budgets; administers staff policies and/or procedures; compiles reports; performs administrative procedures. Research Associate I (L,P,S) Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Gout lab (https://sites.google.com/view/goutlab/home) is hiring a Research Associate in\ncomputational biology to work on two NIH-funded projects in collaboration with the Vermulst lab at University of Southern California (USC). The first project (1R01AG083065) is focused on the potential role of transcription errors on the formation of amyloid and prion-like proteins. The second project is about temporal control of mitochondrial mutagenesis (1R01AG075130-\n01). The candidate will be based in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University, in Starkville, MS (USA) and will collaborate extensively with the Vermulst lab at USC. Postdoctoral Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi An NSF-funded postdoc position is available in the lab of Megan Smith in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University. The project aims to develop robust, user-friendly machine learning tools for population genetic inference and to apply these tools to uncover the drivers of diversification in several empirical systems. The lab has developed a Python package for demographic inference using machine learning, and the successful candidate will extend these methods along several axes.\n\nIn addition to the current project, the lab is pursuing a wide range of empirical and computational research in phylogenetics and population genetics. To learn more about our work visit https://www.meganlsmith.org Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert e0b9226f Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Miami, FL, Florida, United States Miami, FL, Florida, United States First Name (required) 83a2677a Last Name (required) 0f964d09 Email (required) b6b9244a Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance , 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762 Copyright © 2026 Mississippi State University. All Rights Reserved. Technical problems, contact the Service Desk . Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
