    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-full-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-60ac5db6-fe35-496a-848b-aaa2f96a15ef": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate/Full Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant/Associate/Full Professor 511124 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011100 - Plant and Soil Sciences Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Aug 27 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Department of Plant and Soil Sciences in the College of Agriculture and Life Sciences at Mississippi State University is seeking applicants for an Assistant/Associate/Full Professor with a research (70%)/teaching (30%) appointment in corn and small grain agronomics. This position will be a 12-month tenure track appointment with an anticipated start date of January 1, 2027. For candidates with experience or appointment at the Associate or Full Professor levels, the position may also include co-appointment as The Triplett Corn Promotion Board Professor. This Professorship carries the professorship title, and additional salary stipend and some programmatic support. The successful candidate will be expected to collaborate with faculty and staff from the Department of Plant and Soil Sciences as well as with other departments across campus and other institutions. Salary Grade :  UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: Mississippi State is Mississippi's senior comprehensive land-grant institution and has the largest on-campus enrollment (>22,000) of the eight state institutions of higher learning. All components of the university have a strong commitment to teaching, research, and service. The Department of Plant and Soil Sciences has 33 on- and 14 off-campus faculty members engaged in teaching, research, and extension and/or service programs, most of whom carry joint appointments. The programs are supported by state-of-the-art, newly renovated laboratories, equipment, and trained support and professional staff. The department offers Bachelor of Science degrees in Plant and Soil Sciences with Master's and Doctoral graduate students concentrating in Agronomy and, Horticulture. Anticipated Appointment Date: January 1, 2027. Tenure Track Status: Yes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The goal of this position is to develop a nationally recognized research program in the area of applied corn and small grain agronomy and production. The successful candidate will conduct research on cultural practices influencing corn and small grain production systems. Desirable areas of expertise are corn production and agronomy, including crop physiology, crop ecology and tillage systems, soil fertility and nutrient management, modern production practices and precision agriculture, statistical analyses, water or irrigation management, or other agriculture-related science. Regional and multi-state collaboration on research projects is expected as well as the ability to garner extramural funding to support research efforts. Corn is the second highest planted crop acreage in Mississippi. Checkoff funding is available through the Mississippi Corn Promotion Board. The Promotion Board views this position as a priority for the department and producers in the state. The successful candidate will work closely with faculty and staff with multiple departments at Mississippi State University. Teaching responsibilities include a split-level Grain Crops production course as well as active participation in supervising and training graduate students. The incumbent will be expected to teach one additional course suited to the candidate’s experience. Each course will be taught once per year. The successful candidate should possess excellent interpersonal and communication skills, as well as demonstrated experience in design and execution of field and laboratory research. Demonstrated publication experience in refereed journals is critical. Service to the department, college, university, and professional societies is expected. Minimum Qualifications: Earned Ph.D. in Agronomy, Crop or Soil Science or a closely related field from an accredited institution of higher learning is required. Applicants who are “ABD” (All but Dissertation) will be considered. Applicants must have excellent written and oral communication skills. Demonstrated ability of organization and leadership skills are important as well as the willingness to address issues in a team environment. ABDs or degree pending considered (all but DISS): Yes. Preferred Qualifications: A strong background with corn and grain crops and familiarity with modern agricultural production practices. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Applicant must have excellent written and oral communication skills. Excellent organizational and leadership skills are also imperative. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Exposure to educational and agricultural conditions. Lifting, sitting, standing, squatting, etc. will be required. Exposure to chemicals, dust, heat, and cold. Additional exposures may be encountered in a lab setting. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/. Applicants must submit an application online and include a cover letter, CV, transcripts, and names and contact information for three professional references. Any social numbers included on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online. Applicants should submit any questions to: Dr. Michael Mulvaney at mjm1166@msstate.edu or Dr. Michael Cox at msc15@msstate.edu The position will remain open until a suitable candidate is found. Screening Date: October 1, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) bcf78139 Last Name (required) 49c530c5 Email (required) 7fd5071f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Business Manager I, II, or III Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Manages and coordinates the business operations of a department/unit.  Performs duties required to maintain and administer departmental budgets; administers staff policies and/or procedures; compiles reports; performs administrative procedures. Research Associate I (L,P,S) Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Gout lab (https://sites.google.com/view/goutlab/home) is hiring a Research Associate in\ncomputational biology to work on two NIH-funded projects in collaboration with the Vermulst lab at University of Southern California (USC). The first project (1R01AG083065) is focused on the potential role of transcription errors on the formation of amyloid and prion-like proteins. The second project is about temporal control of mitochondrial mutagenesis (1R01AG075130-\n01). The candidate will be based in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University, in Starkville, MS (USA) and will collaborate extensively with the Vermulst lab at USC. Postdoctoral Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi An NSF-funded postdoc position is available in the lab of Megan Smith in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University. The project aims to develop robust, user-friendly machine learning tools for population genetic inference and to apply these tools to uncover the drivers of diversification in several empirical systems. The lab has developed a Python package for demographic inference using machine learning, and the successful candidate will extend these methods along several axes.\n\nIn addition to the current project, the lab is pursuing a wide range of empirical and computational research in phylogenetics and population genetics. To learn more about our work visit https://www.meganlsmith.org Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance ,