    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/postdoctoral-associate-l-p-s-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-96a36763-70d9-4aae-ac6f-74a17732a734": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Postdoctoral Associate (L,P,S) 511152 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 031900 - Chemistry Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The successful candidate will play a leading role in developing innovative optical spectroscopic instrumentation and measurement methodologies, including unpolarized, linearly polarized, and circularly polarized transmission, scattering, photoluminescence, and emerging multimodal spectroscopic platforms. Working closely with faculty collaborators and an interdisciplinary team of postdoctoral associates, graduate students, and undergraduate researchers, the candidate will contribute to cutting-edge research while developing expertise in proposal preparation, project leadership, mentoring, and technology commercialization. The position is particularly suited for candidates pursuing careers in academia, national laboratories, or advanced industrial research. Salary Grade :  UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges. Department Profile: For information on the Department of Chemistry, please visit www.chemistry.msstate.edu Area of Specialization: Chemistry Anticipated Appointment Date: Fall 2026 Tenure Track Status: n/A Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate is expected to become a scientific leader within the research group and will have opportunities to: · Conduct innovative research in optical spectroscopy, scientific instrumentation, and quantitative measurement science. · Publish high-impact research in peer-reviewed journals and present research findings at national and international conferences. · Contribute intellectually to the development of new research directions and interdisciplinary collaborations. · Participate in the preparation of competitive research proposals to federal funding agencies and contribute to long-term strategic research planning. · Mentor graduate and undergraduate researchers while fostering a collaborative, inclusive, and intellectually stimulating research environment. · Contribute to establishing the laboratory as a national leader in next-generation optical measurement science. Minimum Qualifications: · A Ph.D. in Chemistry, Physics, Optical Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Biomedical Engineering, Materials Science, or a closely related discipline (completed before the appointment begins). · Demonstrated research accomplishments in optical spectroscopy, scientific instrumentation, physical chemistry, optical physics, or related fields, as evidenced by peer-reviewed publications. · Strong experimental, analytical, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to conduct independent research. · Excellent written and oral communication skills. Preferred Qualifications: · Quantitative optical measurements involving biological, chemical, or nanomaterial systems · Scientific instrument design, automation, and optical system integration · Computer Programming (Python, LabVIEW,or related languages) · Student mentoring or interdisciplinary collaborative research Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proven ability to work independently and as part of a team. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting and bending. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt chemicals, etc. Instructions for Applying: 1. Cover Letter describing research interests, qualifications, career goals, and including the names and contact information for three professional references. 2. Curriculum Vitae including a complete list of publications and links to representative publications, when available. Restricted Clause: Position is contingent upon continued availability of funding. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Recommended Jobs Business Manager I, II, or III Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Manages and coordinates the business operations of a department/unit.  Performs duties required to maintain and administer departmental budgets; administers staff policies and/or procedures; compiles reports; performs administrative procedures. Research Associate I (L,P,S) Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Gout lab (https://sites.google.com/view/goutlab/home) is hiring a Research Associate in\ncomputational biology to work on two NIH-funded projects in collaboration with the Vermulst lab at University of Southern California (USC). The first project (1R01AG083065) is focused on the potential role of transcription errors on the formation of amyloid and prion-like proteins. The second project is about temporal control of mitochondrial mutagenesis (1R01AG075130-\n01). The candidate will be based in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University, in Starkville, MS (USA) and will collaborate extensively with the Vermulst lab at USC. Postdoctoral Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi An NSF-funded postdoc position is available in the lab of Megan Smith in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University. The project aims to develop robust, user-friendly machine learning tools for population genetic inference and to apply these tools to uncover the drivers of diversification in several empirical systems. The lab has developed a Python package for demographic inference using machine learning, and the successful candidate will extend these methods along several axes.\n\nIn addition to the current project, the lab is pursuing a wide range of empirical and computational research in phylogenetics and population genetics. To learn more about our work visit https://www.meganlsmith.org Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert 3bafe81d Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) 90690930 Last Name (required) 82a9ef36 Email (required) 0773ea95 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences