    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/custodian-i-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-94cae7b8-b50a-42dd-8d35-8fc6dcfe8475": {
      "title": "Custodian I",
      "description": "Custodian I - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Custodian I 511266 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 540100 - Colvard Student Union Support Staff Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 15 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: To perform duties necessary for the routine cleaning and upkeep of buildings. Salary Grade :  CUS-1 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Colvard Student Union is the \"Living Room\" of the university. The CSU hosted more than 4,500 events last year and had 2.1 million people come through its doors. Area of Specialization: Colvard Student Union Essential Duties and Responsibilities: Sweep, dust mop, wet mop and scrub floors. Clean windows, mirrors, walls, doors and other building surfaces. Clean, wax and buff floors. Clean restroom facilities and replenish supplies. Collect trash and empty in trash collection containers. Move furniture, equipment, supplies and other materials as requested. Dust and polish furniture. Report repair needs. Perform minor maintenance and repair duties as directed. May change light bulbs and spray rooms for pests. May vacuum and shampoo carpets. May give work instructions to other Custodians and be responsible for keys and upkeep of a section or a whole building. Minimum Qualifications: Ability to read and write. Ability to work with others and to receive and follow instructions.-or- Any equivalent combination of related experience and/or education approved by the Department of Human Resources Management. Must be able to work nights and weekends. Must be able to lift at least 50lbs. Must be able to be on your feet for long periods of time. Must be able to complete repetitive movements (i.e. stacking and unstacking chairs) Preferred Qualifications: Grade school education. Experience in custodial work Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Teamwork Communication Working Conditions and Physical Effort Regularly involves lifting, bending or other physical exertion. Often exposed to one or more elements such as heat, cold, noise, dust, dirt, chemicals, etc. Occasional-Routine deadlines; usually sufficient lead time; variance in work volume seasonal and predictable; priorities can be anticipated; some interruptions are present; travel or other inconveniences have advance notice; involves occasional exposure to demands and pressures from persons other than immediate supervisor. Job frequently requires standing, walking, reaching, climbing or balancing, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands, and lifting up to 25 pounds. Job occasionally requires sitting, stooping/kneeling/crouching/crawling, and lifting more than 100 pounds. Vision requirements: Ability to see information in print and/or electronically. Instructions for Applying: Submit application online. Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disa