    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/enterprise-software-developer-ii-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states": {
      "title": "Enterprise Software Developer II",
      "description": "Enterprise Software Developer II - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Enterprise Software Developer II 511249 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 460100 - Enterprise Information Systems Professional Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 14 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: This position will work as a team member in Enterprise Information Systems at Mississippi State University. The Software Developer supports the University community by developing, coordinating, and managing enterprise application software systems and enterprise data by providing critical information services to our clients. Salary Grade :  15 Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: • Design, develop, and maintain custom programming to assist with internal processes and import/export data to/from MSU’s ERP system (Banner). • Provide technical assistance by responding to inquiries from others regarding errors, problems, or questions about Banner and related Enterprise Applications. • Create and maintain documentation that describes programs, operating procedures, and installations, including but not limited to, internal knowledge base, solutions, and project updates. • Assist with the administration, maintenance, and support of Ellucian products and integrated software to third party systems. • Stay updated on industry-wide changes, participate in technical user groups, and attend relevant training classes • Research and solve problems both independently and as a member of a team. • Monitor, track, and report project risks, issues, milestones, and work completed. • Consult with administrators to gather information to evaluate procedures and business needs. • Identify inefficiencies and makes suggestions based on analysis, system capabilities and available resources. • Continually upgrade knowledge of new tools and technologies. Supervisory Responsibility: None. Minimum Qualifications: Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, Computer Engineering or related area from an accredited institution AND two years of relevant work experience. Required Qualifications: • Experience in developing business software using industry development tools. • Knowledge and skill interviewing clients to understand their business needs and translate them into software specifications. • Knowledge and skill in analyzing business processes in multiple areas. • Work in a team and project driven environment. Any equivalent combination of related education and related experience may be considered. Preferred Qualifications: • Two years’ experience working in enterprise systems in the higher education environment. • Two years’ experience working with Oracle SQL and related database analysis tools. • Experience with ERP systems. • Experience in object-oriented programming, using one or more of the following languages: Java/J2EE, Groovy, Ruby, Python, and .NET • Experience in full stack development using languages and frameworks such as Angular, React, JavaScript, AJAX, HTML, and XML. • Experience programming using web application frameworks such as Spring, Grails, and Rails. • Knowledge of development environment tools such as Eclipse, IntelliJ, Subversion, Maven, and Ant. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: • Experience in developing business software using industry development tools. • Knowledge and skill interviewing clients to understand their business needs and translate them into software specifications. • Knowledge and skill in analyzing business processes in multiple areas. • Work in a team and project driven environment. Working Conditions and Physical Effort No unusual physical requirements. Requires limited lifting of files and records and nearly all work is performed in a comfortable indoor facility. Frequent external imposed deadlines; set and revised beyond one’s control; interruptions influence priorities; difficult to anticipate nature or volume of work with certainty beyond a few days; meeting of deadlines and coordination of unrelated activities are key to position; involves conflict-resolution or similar interactions involving emotional issues or stress on a regular basis. Job frequently requires walking, sitting, reaching, talking, hearing, handling objects with hands. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ All applicants must apply online at www.msujobs.msstate.edu by attaching a cover letter and resume which includes the names and addresses of 3 professional references. We will accept applications only from persons with indefinite employment authorization in the U.S., and will not sponsor for nonimmigrant or immigrant status for this position. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Back to job listing Apply Now First Name (required) 8a489374 Last Name (required) 3e8f7cad Email (required) aa8ff0ef Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Business Manager I, II, or III Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Manages and coordinates the business operations of a department/unit.  Performs duties required to maintain and administer departmental budgets; administers staff policies and/or procedures; compiles reports; performs administrative procedures. Research Associate I (L,P,S) Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Gout lab (https://sites.google.com/view/goutlab/home) is hiring a Research Associate in\ncomputational biology to work on two NIH-funded projects in collaboration with the Vermulst lab at University of Southern California (USC). The first project (1R01AG083065) is focused on the potential role of transcription errors on the formation of amyloid and prion-like proteins. The second project is about temporal control of mitochondrial mutagenesis (1R01AG075130-\n01). The candidate will be based in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University, in Starkville, MS (USA) and will collaborate extensively with the Vermulst lab at USC. Postdoctoral Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi An NSF-funded postdoc position is available in the lab of Megan Smith in the Department of Biological Sciences at Mississippi State University. The project aims to develop robust, user-friendly machine learning tools for population genetic inference and to apply these tools to uncover the drivers of diversification in several empirical systems. The lab has developed a Python package for demographic inference using machine learning, and the successful candidate will extend these methods along several axes.\n\nIn addition to the current project, the lab is pursuing a wide range of empirical and computational research in phylogenetics and population genetics. To learn more about our work visit https://www.meganlsmith.org Sign Up for Job Alerts Job Alert d1b82a13 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Professional Professional Employment Type Regular Full-Time 12-month Regular Full-Time 12-month Locations Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States First Name (required) ecbfa3e3 Last Name (required) d2279b3a Email (required) 9d38eb16 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance , 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762 Copyright © 2026 Mississippi State University. All Rights Reserved. Technical problems, contact the Service Desk . Candidate Details We use cooki