    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-6fb8d7d1-8d74-4272-9462-b86f9d721458": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor 511185 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 011900 - Agricultural Science & Plant Protec Faculty Regular Full-Time 12-month Opening on: Sep 24 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: The Department of Agricultural Science and Plant Protection (ASPP) at Mississippi State University seeks to fill a full-time, 12-month Assistant Professor position in Weed Science based in Starkville on the main campus. The position will carry a 100% Extension, tenure-track appointment and will provide statewide leadership for science-based weed management in all major row crops grown in Mississippi, complementing existing Weed Science programs. The program will serve county Extension personnel, producers, consultants, agricultural retailers, pesticide applicators, industry, agencies, and additional stakeholders. Salary Grade :  UC Please see Staff Compensation Structure or Skilled Crafts and Service Maintenance Compensation Schedule for salary ranges.  For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Agricultural Science and Plant Protection has academic, research, and Extension education missions within the land-grant tradition. The department includes expertise in entomology, plant pathology, weed science, and interdisciplinary agricultural science and supports undergraduate, graduate, research, and statewide Extension programs. Area of Specialization: Extension Row Crop Weed Scientist Anticipated Appointment Date: May 1, 2027. Tenure Track Status: Yes. Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The successful candidate will develop and lead an applied Extension Weed Science program responsive to Mississippi stakeholder needs. Responsibilities will include integrated weed management; herbicide stewardship and resistance management; diagnosis and response to emerging weed control problems; county agent training; field demonstrations; Extension publications and digital resources; peer-reviewed publications; and collaboration with state, regional, and national partners. The incumbent will conduct applied research and field demonstrations to support science-based Extension suggestions and will pursue external funding to strengthen the program. Close collaboration with ASPP Weed Science faculty, county Extension personnel, research and Extension centers, commodity groups, consultants, agricultural retailers, and industry is expected. Graduate and undergraduate student mentoring, guest instruction, committee service, and additional academic contributions are expected. Minimum Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Weed Science, Agronomy, Plant Science, Crop Science, or a closely related field with substantial training in weed management is required by the date of appointment (or “all but dissertation” completed and graduation imminent). Candidates must demonstrate excellent written and oral communication skills, strong interpersonal skills, and the ability to translate research-based information into effective Extension education and suggestions for agricultural audiences. ABDs or degree pending considered (all but DISS): Yes. Preferred Qualifications: Experience in Extension or applied outreach; demonstrated expertise in integrated weed management, herbicide resistance, herbicide stewardship, agronomic crop production, or other weed-management systems relevant to Mississippi; experience working with county agents, producers, consultants, agricultural retailers, and industry; evidence of multidisciplinary collaboration; experience obtaining extramural support; and a record of effective educational communication. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Ability to develop and evaluate Extension programs; communicate technical information to diverse audiences; diagnose field weed-management problems; work effectively in interdisciplinary teams; coordinate statewide activities; manage multiple projects and deadlines; and build productive relationships with Extension personnel and agricultural stakeholders. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Frequent travel within Mississippi and outdoor field work are expected. Duties may include work in hot and humid conditions, walking over uneven agricultural terrain, participation in field days and demonstrations, working with agricultural equipment, and movement of field or demonstration materials. Instructions for Applying: Link to apply: http://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/ Applications must be submitted through the Human Resources Management website at https://www.jobs.msstate.edu by completing the professional application and submitting a cover letter, current curriculum vitae, a statement of teaching philosophy and research interests, copies of up to three relevant publications, contact information for three references, and a current transcript. Any social numbers included on requested transcripts should be redacted prior to submitting online. An official transcript will be required if selected for an interview. For additional questions, please contact Swayze Hollenhead at sh1270@msstate.edu. Screening Date: October 8, 2026, until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Recommended Jobs Office Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Performs a variety of basic to complex office support and/or secretarial duties primarily related to travel arrangements and expenditures, which require a range of skills and knowledge of organizational policies and procedures. Assistant Professor Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychology, full-time, 9-month, tenure track, beginning August 16, 2027. Campus Transit Bus Driver Rehire Retiree Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi To drive a campus transit bus to transport passengers around Starkville/MSU area. Mississippi State, MS 39762 Phone: (662)325-2323 Facebook Instagram X Youtube Pinterest Cookie Preferences Customer Service at MSState | EEO Statement at MSState | Ethics Line at MSState | Legal Notices at MSState | Annual Security & Fire Report at MSState Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance , 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762 Copyright © 2026 Mississippi State University. All Rights Reserved. Technical problems, contact the Service Desk . Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all"
    },
    "https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu/jobs/assistant-professor-main-campus-starkville-ms-mississippi-united-states-e200fc41-e951-43c5-b769-b3f7f67a6eff": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor",
      "description": "Assistant Professor - Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi, United States Learn More about MSU Home Benefits & Perks Work/Life Balance About Starkville Applicant Notices Campus Security My Profile Applicant Login Kiosk mode We're Hiring! Assistant Professor 511257 Main Campus - Starkville, MS Mississippi - Main Campus 038600 - Psychology Faculty Regular Full-Time 9-month Opening on: Sep 23 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Function: Assistant Professor in the Department of Psychology, full-time, 9-month, tenure track, beginning August 16, 2027. Salary Grade :  UC For salary grade UC, these positions are \"Unclassified\" and salary ranges are determined by the hiring department. Department Profile: The Department of Psychology is within the College of Arts & Sciences. It houses 24 full time faculty members, 800 undergraduates, and about 40 doctoral students in our Cognitive Science and Clinical Psychology Ph.D. programs. Area of Specialization: Clinical Psychology or Closely Related Field Anticipated Appointment Date: August 16, 2026 Tenure Track Status: Tenure-Track Essential Duties and Responsibilities: The new faculty member will teach undergraduate and graduate courses, including courses in the specialty area of clinical psychology. The successful applicants will maintain a program of scholarly research, apply for external funding, teach undergraduates and graduate courses, and supervise graduate students. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must have completed a doctoral degree from an APA, CPA, or PCSAS accredited program by the time of appointment and be eligible for eventual licensure in Mississippi. Working Conditions and Physical Effort Work takes place in an office environment. Instructions for Applying: Interested applicants must apply online at https://explore.msujobs.msstate.edu and attach a cover letter; curriculum vitae; statements on research and teaching; up to three pre/reprints; and contact information for at least three professional references. Review of applications will begin October 15, 2026, but applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Questions about the position can be directed to the search committee chair, Dr. Ty Stafford tws37@msstate.edu. Equal Employment Opportunity Statement: Mississippi State University is an equal opportunity institution. Discrimination is prohibited in university employment, programs or activities based on race, color, ethnicity, sex, pregnancy, religion, national origin, disability, age, sexual orientation, genetic information, status as a U.S. veteran, or any other status to the extent protected by applicable law. Questions about equal opportunity programs or compliance should be directed to the Office of Civil Rights Compliance, 231 Famous Maroon Band Street, P.O. 6044, Mississippi State, MS 39762, (662) 325-5839. What do I do if I need an accommodation? In compliance with the ADA Amendments Act (ADA), if you have a disability and would like to request an accommodation in order to apply for a position with Mississippi State University, please contact the Department of Human Resources Management at tel: (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . If you have any questions regarding this policy, contact the Department of Human Resources Management at (662) 325-3713 or ada@hrm.msstate.edu . Upon request, sections of this job listing are available in large print, and readers are available to assist the visually impaired. Recommended Jobs Office Associate Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi Performs a variety of basic to complex office support and/or secretarial duties primarily related to travel arrangements and expenditures, which require a range of skills and knowledge of organizational policies and procedures. Assistant Professor Main Campus - Starkville, MS, Mississippi The Department of Agricultural Science and Plant Protection (ASPP) at Mississippi State University seeks to fill a full-time, 12-month Assistant Pr